  "reading": "L5 is not patient at a level: 75.1% of its price clusters are a single print, a follow-on print at the same level arrives p50 1 s / p90 7 s after the previous one, and only 1.8% of follow-on prints (3.3% of follow-on dollars) arrive more than 30 s later. L5's NEXT print is at a different price after a median 6 s (p75 20 s, p90 47 s) with a median step of 2 c (22151 paid more, 23187 paid less); 83.5% of those reprices happen inside our 30 s deadline. Ours: 9 of 45 orders filled (time to fill p50 11.65 s, max 24.453 s), 23 cancelled untouched at the 30 s deadline, 3 repriced, 10 post-only rejects. The mismatch is therefore NOT rest length: L5 would rarely have rested 30 s at one price. It is reprice cadence -- L5 moves its price within seconds when the touch moves, while we hold one price for the full deadline, cancel, and only re-decide on the next cycle (23 of our 45 orders ended that way). Executable lever: a touch-following reprice inside the rest window (the 'repriced:touch_moved' path exists and fired 3 times); the 30 s deadline itself is a frozen rung parameter. Reported, not changed."
 },
